WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.794
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:05.837
Sammy.

00:00:06.296 --> 00:00:08.173
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:09.055
Go!

00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:14.095
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.406
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.476 --> 00:00:20.650
This is dad's book.

00:00:20.685 --> 00:00:22.771
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:22.806 --> 00:00:24.814
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:26.399
The family business.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:27.866
I got to find dad.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.153
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:58.341 --> 00:01:59.724
I know you're just doing your job

00:01:59.759 --> 00:02:02.073
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:02.108 --> 00:02:04.353
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:04.388 --> 00:02:07.350
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:07.385 --> 00:02:08.809
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.403
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:12.538 --> 00:02:16.337
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:16.372 --> 00:02:19.003
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.130
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:21.165 --> 00:02:23.295
I was up late...

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.391
Watching TV.

00:02:25.426 --> 00:02:27.178
When I heard this...

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.978
Weird noise.

00:02:29.013 --> 00:02:32.078
What did it sound like?

00:02:32.113 --> 00:02:35.144
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:36.604 --> 00:02:39.815
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.525
Um...

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:45.035
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.093
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:02:47.128 --> 00:02:49.081
So much better than the original?

00:02:49.116 --> 00:02:49.900
Totally.

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:52.298
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:02:52.488 --> 00:02:53.794
Yuck.

00:02:53.829 --> 00:02:55.513
That's what I mean.

00:02:57.917 --> 00:02:59.133
Evan?

00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:01.879
Did you see what this thing was?

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.253
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:04.288 --> 00:03:06.592
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:06.993 --> 00:03:08.204
Then what?

00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:12.354
It took him away.

00:03:12.389 --> 00:03:15.621
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:15.656 --> 00:03:18.527
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.398
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:21.956 --> 00:03:26.111
Like this whining growl.

00:03:29.016 --> 00:03:30.449
Thanks for your time.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.331
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:37.966 --> 00:03:39.798
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:40.572 --> 00:03:42.461
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:03:43.196 --> 00:03:45.246
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:03:45.281 --> 00:03:46.765
Yeah, maybe not.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.214
Except for this.

00:03:48.249 --> 00:03:50.425
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.129
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:03:53.164 --> 00:03:54.971
Why would he even do that?

00:03:55.006 --> 00:03:59.260
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:03:59.295 --> 00:04:01.888
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:04:01.923 --> 00:04:03.521
He found this too.

00:04:03.556 --> 00:04:08.687
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:09.104 --> 00:04:10.078
It is weird.

00:04:10.563 --> 00:04:11.450
Yeah.

00:04:11.523 --> 00:04:14.491
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:16.044
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:17.563
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:17.564 --> 00:04:21.908
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:21.943 --> 00:04:24.077
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:24.112 --> 00:04:27.163
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:27.198 --> 00:04:28.623
Right.

00:04:29.666 --> 00:04:32.043
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:32.078 --> 00:04:33.593
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:33.628 --> 00:04:35.547
Let's have another round?

00:04:35.713 --> 00:04:37.138
We should get an early start.

00:04:37.173 --> 00:04:40.343
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:04:42.261 --> 00:04:43.375
You're right.

00:04:44.463 --> 00:04:46.444
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:34.222 --> 00:06:35.605
Hey, hey.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.519
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:39.936 --> 00:06:41.104
Sam?

00:06:43.815 --> 00:06:45.176
Sammy!

00:07:04.503 --> 00:07:06.088
Sam...

00:07:17.766 --> 00:07:20.811
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:20.846 --> 00:07:22.736
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:22.771 --> 00:07:25.899
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:28.318
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:28.353 --> 00:07:30.035
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:33.198
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:33.233 --> 00:07:35.081
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:38.060
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:38.095 --> 00:07:40.661
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:40.903 --> 00:07:43.833
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:07:45.794 --> 00:07:47.712
All right. What's his name?

00:07:47.747 --> 00:07:49.214
Winchester.

00:07:50.465 --> 00:07:51.966
Sam Winchester.

00:07:52.508 --> 00:07:53.694
Like the riffle?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.387
Like the riffle.

00:07:55.512 --> 00:07:57.103
Winchester, Sam

00:08:02.018 --> 00:08:03.985
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:09.651
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:09.818 --> 00:08:12.654
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:13.251 --> 00:08:14.906
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:15.508 --> 00:08:17.701
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:17.736 --> 00:08:19.232
Handsome though.

00:08:24.259 --> 00:08:26.042
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:26.077 --> 00:08:28.155
I already have a lead.

00:08:28.816 --> 00:08:31.047
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:31.082 --> 00:08:32.582
County traffic cam.

00:08:32.617 --> 00:08:33.774
Right, yeah.

00:08:33.809 --> 00:08:35.427
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:35.462 --> 00:08:37.470
Oh, whoever.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.890
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:40.925 --> 00:08:43.723
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:08:43.758 --> 00:08:46.521
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:08:46.556 --> 00:08:50.442
Won't you fill out...

00:08:51.178 --> 00:08:52.993
A missing persons report.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:57.949
And sit tight over here.

00:08:58.805 --> 00:09:00.243
Officer, look uh...

00:09:01.432 --> 00:09:02.516
He's family.

00:09:03.156 --> 00:09:04.170
And I kind of...

00:09:05.134 --> 00:09:06.131
Look out for the kid.

00:09:07.074 --> 00:09:08.439
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:08.944 --> 00:09:10.411
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:12.221 --> 00:09:13.729
Well, tell me something.

00:09:13.764 --> 00:09:16.642
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:16.677 --> 00:09:19.478
Any of them come back?

00:09:20.187 --> 00:09:23.816
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:23.851 --> 00:09:26.151
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:12.556 --> 00:10:13.689
Greg.

00:10:13.724 --> 00:10:15.559
I think we've got something.

00:10:16.768 --> 00:10:18.979
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:19.014 --> 00:10:21.279
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:21.314 --> 00:10:25.902
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:26.653 --> 00:10:28.084
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:28.119 --> 00:10:28.812
Just wait, wait.

00:10:28.857 --> 00:10:30.038
Next one.

00:10:30.073 --> 00:10:33.201
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:33.236 --> 00:10:35.996
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:36.663 --> 00:10:39.207
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.427
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:10:43.462 --> 00:10:47.716
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:10:54.473 --> 00:10:55.673
Do you hear that engine?

00:10:55.708 --> 00:10:56.939
Yeah.

00:10:57.893 --> 00:11:00.812
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:11:01.229 --> 00:11:03.148
Sure.

00:11:05.525 --> 00:11:07.486
I'll be damned.

00:11:22.417 --> 00:11:24.294
You're alive?

00:11:25.128 --> 00:11:26.428
Hey, you okay?

00:11:26.463 --> 00:11:29.424
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:30.552 --> 00:11:31.655
Where are we?

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:33.220
I don't know.

00:11:33.903 --> 00:11:35.103
Country, I think.

00:11:35.757 --> 00:11:37.328
Smells like the country.

00:11:38.002 --> 00:11:39.518
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:40.054 --> 00:11:40.977
Yeah.

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:44.272
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:45.400
Oh, yeah?

00:11:45.435 --> 00:11:46.197
Yeah.

00:11:46.232 --> 00:11:49.826
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:11:49.861 --> 00:11:53.406
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:11:53.441 --> 00:11:55.551
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:11:55.586 --> 00:11:57.626
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:11:57.661 --> 00:12:00.580
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:12:00.615 --> 00:12:02.339
What are they?

00:12:03.061 --> 00:12:03.775
Have you seen them?

00:12:04.476 --> 00:12:04.702
What are you talking about?

00:12:04.703 --> 00:12:06.586
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:06.621 --> 00:12:08.338
See for yourself.

00:12:27.482 --> 00:12:28.615
Leave me alone.

00:12:29.384 --> 00:12:31.278
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:12:48.619 --> 00:12:50.788
I'll be damned.

00:12:53.624 --> 00:12:55.216
They're just people.

00:12:55.251 --> 00:12:58.504
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:12:58.921 --> 00:13:00.568
How often do they feed you?

00:13:00.603 --> 00:13:01.691
Once a day.

00:13:02.008 --> 00:13:05.511
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.055
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.474
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:10.509 --> 00:13:12.410
Waiting for what?

00:13:12.445 --> 00:13:14.276
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:14.311 --> 00:13:16.536
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:16.571 --> 00:13:17.303
Oh, yeah?

00:13:17.338 --> 00:13:17.738
Yeah.

00:13:17.773 --> 00:13:19.028
What do you they want then?

00:13:19.685 --> 00:13:21.575
Depends on who they are.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:24.613
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:24.648 --> 00:13:27.366
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:41.752 --> 00:13:43.973
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:13:44.008 --> 00:13:47.595
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.572
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:13:50.016 --> 00:13:51.480
I don't see any other roads here.

00:13:51.911 --> 00:13:56.020
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:13:56.523 --> 00:13:57.855
Great.

00:14:10.723 --> 00:14:12.077
So, Gregory.

00:14:12.593 --> 00:14:13.085
Yeah.

00:14:13.887 --> 00:14:15.128
I ran your badge number.

00:14:15.163 --> 00:14:17.860
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:17.895 --> 00:14:19.752
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:20.445 --> 00:14:23.589
And they just got back to me...

00:14:27.213 --> 00:14:29.386
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:30.172 --> 00:14:33.377
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:39.425
I lost some weight.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.807
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:41.842 --> 00:14:42.585
Okay.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.100
Would you step out of the car please?

00:14:44.135 --> 00:14:45.003
Look, look, look.

00:14:47.053 --> 00:14:49.222
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:14:49.257 --> 00:14:51.433
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:14:51.468 --> 00:14:53.608
But first please...

00:14:53.643 --> 00:14:54.635
Let me find Sam.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.192
I don't even know who you are.

00:14:56.514 --> 00:14:58.696
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:14:58.731 --> 00:15:01.067
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:15:01.102 --> 00:15:04.561
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:05.607 --> 00:15:07.273
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:07.564 --> 00:15:09.416
When we were young...

00:15:09.451 --> 00:15:12.458
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:13.496 --> 00:15:16.635
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:17.097 --> 00:15:20.628
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:22.672 --> 00:15:26.968
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:29.888
Please...

00:15:30.346 --> 00:15:33.308
He's my family.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.234
I'm sorry.

00:15:36.269 --> 00:15:38.730
You've given me no choice.

00:15:38.765 --> 00:15:41.191
I have to take you in.

00:15:54.897 --> 00:15:57.838
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:16:00.543 --> 00:16:02.072
What's your name again?

00:16:02.107 --> 00:16:03.382
It's Sam.

00:16:03.946 --> 00:16:07.325
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:08.951
Don't...

00:16:09.535 --> 00:16:11.078
Call me...

00:16:11.113 --> 00:16:12.621
Sammy.

00:16:15.082 --> 00:16:17.460
What is it?

00:16:21.464 --> 00:16:22.805
It's a bracket.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:26.594
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:28.888 --> 00:16:31.474
Must have been a short.

00:16:34.226 --> 00:16:37.521
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:40.399 --> 00:16:42.117
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:16:42.152 --> 00:16:42.711
What?

00:16:43.187 --> 00:16:44.869
This isn't right.

00:16:44.904 --> 00:16:46.885
Do you want to get out of here?

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.831
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:16:48.866 --> 00:16:51.077
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:16:51.112 --> 00:16:51.934
Okay. Don't worry.

00:16:51.969 --> 00:16:52.629
No.

00:16:52.664 --> 00:16:55.456
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:16:55.491 --> 00:16:57.416
Bye, Sammy.

00:16:57.708 --> 00:16:59.627
Jenkins!

00:17:39.416 --> 00:17:41.376
Thank you.

00:19:14.444 --> 00:19:16.195
Okay, officer.

00:19:16.446 --> 00:19:18.021
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:18.056 --> 00:19:19.976
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:20.276 --> 00:19:21.909
Right.

00:19:22.201 --> 00:19:24.078
I was wondering...

00:19:24.328 --> 00:19:26.726
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:26.761 --> 00:19:29.125
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:30.042 --> 00:19:33.379
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:33.414 --> 00:19:35.763
A lot like Sam.

00:19:35.798 --> 00:19:37.675
We searched for him but...

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:39.927
Nothing.

00:19:40.595 --> 00:19:43.514
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:19:43.549 --> 00:19:45.850
And for them...

00:19:48.436 --> 00:19:51.006
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:19:54.567 --> 00:19:56.792
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:08.551 --> 00:20:10.718
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:11.792 --> 00:20:13.544
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:13.579 --> 00:20:14.680
No way.

00:20:14.715 --> 00:20:15.781
Hey...

00:20:16.464 --> 00:20:18.278
You're a civilian.

00:20:18.313 --> 00:20:20.057
And a felon, I think.

00:20:20.092 --> 00:20:22.511
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:23.037 --> 00:20:24.388
You're not going without me.

00:20:27.624 --> 00:20:29.775
All right. You promise...

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:33.064
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:33.703 --> 00:20:35.041
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:35.076 --> 00:20:36.984
Shake on it.

00:20:40.911 --> 00:20:42.782
Oh, come on.

00:20:43.532 --> 00:20:45.833
This is ridiculous.

00:20:46.568 --> 00:20:48.612
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:20:48.647 --> 00:20:51.990
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:20:55.452 --> 00:20:58.372
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:28.985 --> 00:21:30.391
Hello?

00:21:33.615 --> 00:21:35.463
Anybody home?

00:21:50.424 --> 00:21:51.668
Hi.

00:21:53.009 --> 00:21:54.780
How are you?

00:22:00.559 --> 00:22:02.234
Who are you?

00:22:02.269 --> 00:22:06.565
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.608
What's your name?

00:22:08.643 --> 00:22:10.242
Missy.

00:22:10.277 --> 00:22:12.737
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:12.772 --> 00:22:15.198
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:15.233 --> 00:22:17.624
She's dead.

00:22:17.659 --> 00:22:21.496
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:21.788 --> 00:22:24.082
No?

00:22:25.125 --> 00:22:28.170
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:28.587 --> 00:22:30.922
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:30.957 --> 00:22:33.357
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:35.469 --> 00:22:37.825
Look at that picture.

00:22:39.848 --> 00:22:41.356
What?

00:22:41.391 --> 00:22:43.894
That's gonna hurt.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:48.363
Missy, sweetheart.

00:22:48.398 --> 00:22:50.901
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:22:50.936 --> 00:22:53.487
Yes, daddy.

00:23:10.212 --> 00:23:12.589
Son of a bitch.

00:24:16.226 --> 00:24:18.467
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:18.502 --> 00:24:21.783
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:36.830 --> 00:24:39.208
You all right?

00:24:42.252 --> 00:24:45.213
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:24:45.248 --> 00:24:47.003
Yeah.

00:24:47.038 --> 00:24:48.759
You're...

00:24:49.134 --> 00:24:52.471
You're cousin's looking for you.

00:24:53.555 --> 00:24:55.411
Thank God.

00:24:55.446 --> 00:24:57.482
Where is he?

00:24:57.517 --> 00:24:59.519
He uh...

00:24:59.853 --> 00:25:03.065
I cuffed him to my car.

00:25:24.670 --> 00:25:26.421
Sam?

00:25:27.047 --> 00:25:28.382
Are you hurt?

00:25:28.417 --> 00:25:30.133
No.

00:25:30.342 --> 00:25:32.844
Damn, it's good to see you.

00:25:33.595 --> 00:25:36.682
How did you get out of the cuffs?

00:25:36.717 --> 00:25:39.559
I know a trick or two.

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:42.521
All right.

00:25:42.771 --> 00:25:44.231
Oh.

00:25:44.523 --> 00:25:46.865
These locks they're gonna be a bitch.

00:25:46.900 --> 00:25:50.112
Well, there's some kind of
automatic control. Right there.

00:25:50.347 --> 00:25:52.188
Have you seen them?

00:25:52.223 --> 00:25:53.488
Yeah.

00:25:53.523 --> 00:25:55.734
Dude, they're just people.

00:25:55.769 --> 00:25:57.826
And they jumped you?

00:25:57.861 --> 00:26:01.364
Must be getting a little
rusty there, kiddo.

00:26:01.399 --> 00:26:02.386
What do they want?

00:26:02.421 --> 00:26:03.150
I don't know.

00:26:03.151 --> 00:26:05.010
They let Jenkins go, but...

00:26:05.045 --> 00:26:06.835
That was some sort of trap.

00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:08.947
It doesn't make any sense to me.

00:26:08.982 --> 00:26:10.337
Oh, well that's the point.

00:26:10.372 --> 00:26:11.548
You know with...

00:26:11.583 --> 00:26:15.587
Our usual play mates there's rules,
here's patterns. But with people...

00:26:15.622 --> 00:26:17.429
They're just crazy.

00:26:17.464 --> 00:26:20.008
You see anything else out there?

00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:23.365
He has about a dozen junk cars
out back. Plates from all over.

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:25.930
So, I'm thinking when they take
someone they take their car too.

00:26:25.965 --> 00:26:30.060
Did you see a black mustang?
Out there about ten years old?

00:26:30.095 --> 00:26:33.605
Yeah, actually I did.

00:26:35.281 --> 00:26:38.284
Your brothers?

00:26:39.494 --> 00:26:41.955
I'm sorry.

00:26:43.247 --> 00:26:46.334
Let's get you guys out of here. Then
we'll take care of those bastards.

00:26:46.369 --> 00:26:48.503
It takes a key, key?

00:26:48.538 --> 00:26:49.844
I don't know.

00:26:49.879 --> 00:26:51.756
All right, I better go find it.

00:26:51.791 --> 00:26:53.424
Hey.

00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:55.718
Be careful.

00:26:55.953 --> 00:26:57.920
Yeah.

00:28:09.325 --> 00:28:11.327
Well, I'll say it again.

00:28:11.362 --> 00:28:13.954
Demons I get.

00:28:14.121 --> 00:28:16.540
People are crazy.

00:29:06.420 --> 00:29:08.026
What the...

00:30:43.986 --> 00:30:46.656
It's okay. I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:30:46.989 --> 00:30:48.699
I know.

00:30:48.908 --> 00:30:50.201
Daddy!

00:30:50.326 --> 00:30:51.661
Daddy!

00:30:51.911 --> 00:30:53.454
Daddy!

00:30:54.080 --> 00:30:55.915
Daddy!

00:31:24.326 --> 00:31:27.413
I'm gonna kick your ass first.

00:31:27.746 --> 00:31:29.665
Then yours.

00:31:41.552 --> 00:31:43.345
Come on.

00:31:43.512 --> 00:31:44.895
Let's hunt.

00:31:44.930 --> 00:31:46.890
Yeah, this one's a fighter.

00:31:46.925 --> 00:31:49.893
Sure be fun to hunt.

00:31:50.561 --> 00:31:52.444
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:31:52.479 --> 00:31:54.565
This is what this is about? You...

00:31:54.600 --> 00:31:57.401
You yahoos hunt people?

00:31:58.902 --> 00:32:02.364
You ever killed before?

00:32:02.399 --> 00:32:04.366
What?

00:32:05.659 --> 00:32:08.287
Well, it depends on what you mean.

00:32:08.322 --> 00:32:11.630
I've hunted all my life.

00:32:11.665 --> 00:32:15.377
Just like my father, his before him.

00:32:15.412 --> 00:32:17.504
I've hunted deer...

00:32:17.539 --> 00:32:19.304
And bear...

00:32:19.339 --> 00:32:23.385
I even got a coo-Coo once. Oh boy.

00:32:23.802 --> 00:32:26.597
But the best hunt...

00:32:26.632 --> 00:32:29.099
Is human.

00:32:30.267 --> 00:32:33.068
Oh, there's nothing like it.

00:32:33.103 --> 00:32:37.573
Holding their life in your hands.

00:32:37.608 --> 00:32:42.529
Seeing the fear in their
eyes just before they go dark.

00:32:42.564 --> 00:32:46.450
Makes you feel powerful alive.

00:32:46.685 --> 00:32:49.403
You're a sick puppy.

00:32:50.070 --> 00:32:52.246
We give them a weapon.

00:32:52.281 --> 00:32:55.158
Give him a fighting chance.

00:32:55.393 --> 00:32:57.701
It's kind of like...

00:32:57.736 --> 00:33:00.745
Our tradition passed down

00:33:00.780 --> 00:33:06.001
Father to son, cost
only one or two a year.

00:33:06.036 --> 00:33:11.082
Never enough to bring the lot
down we've never been that sloppy.

00:33:11.117 --> 00:33:13.627
Yeah, well. Don't save yourself short.

00:33:13.662 --> 00:33:16.338
You're plenty of sloppy.

00:33:17.672 --> 00:33:21.635
So what? You're with that pretty cop?

00:33:26.932 --> 00:33:29.935
Are you a cop?

00:33:31.561 --> 00:33:34.112
If I tell you...

00:33:34.147 --> 00:33:38.026
You promise not to make
me into an ash tray?

00:33:42.288 --> 00:33:45.875
Only reason I don't let my
boys take you right here now

00:33:45.910 --> 00:33:49.385
Is that there's
something I need to know.

00:33:49.420 --> 00:33:52.206
Yeah, how about it's not
nice to marry your sister.

00:33:53.077 --> 00:33:58.763
Tell me, any of the cops
go come looking for you?

00:33:58.798 --> 00:34:00.104
Oh, eat me.

00:34:00.139 --> 00:34:03.434
No, no, no. Wait. You actually might.

00:34:05.937 --> 00:34:08.821
You think this is funny?

00:34:08.856 --> 00:34:12.777
You've brought this down on my family.

00:34:14.520 --> 00:34:16.487
All right?

00:34:16.522 --> 00:34:19.546
You want to play games?

00:34:19.581 --> 00:34:22.570
We'll play some games.

00:34:24.864 --> 00:34:29.577
Looks like we're gonna have a
hunt tonight after all, boys.

00:34:29.612 --> 00:34:32.663
And you get to pick the animal.

00:34:32.698 --> 00:34:35.037
The boy or the cop.

00:34:35.072 --> 00:34:37.376
Okay, wait, wait.

00:34:37.960 --> 00:34:40.838
Look, nobody's coming for
me. All right? It's just us.

00:34:40.873 --> 00:34:44.091
You don't choose, I will.

00:34:45.635 --> 00:34:49.055
Oh, you son of a bitch!

00:34:53.726 --> 00:34:56.402
Next time, I'll take an eye.

00:34:56.437 --> 00:35:00.233
All right, all right. The
guy. The guy. Take the guy!

00:35:00.858 --> 00:35:02.617
Lee.

00:35:02.952 --> 00:35:05.412
Go do it.

00:35:05.955 --> 00:35:08.561
Don't let him out though.

00:35:08.596 --> 00:35:11.168
Shoot him in the cage.

00:35:12.294 --> 00:35:14.338
What?

00:35:14.547 --> 00:35:16.323
I thought you said you
were gonna hunt him.

00:35:16.358 --> 00:35:17.589
You're gonna give him a chance!

00:35:17.624 --> 00:35:19.161
Lee!

00:35:19.196 --> 00:35:21.053
When you're done with the boy.

00:35:21.088 --> 00:35:24.014
Shoot the bitch too.

00:35:26.350 --> 00:35:31.814
We're cleaning this mess up before
any more cops come running out here.

00:35:40.614 --> 00:35:42.491
What are you doing?

00:35:50.624 --> 00:35:51.792
Hey!

00:35:53.836 --> 00:35:56.297
You hurt my brother,
I'll kill you. I swear.

00:35:56.332 --> 00:35:58.712
I'll kill you all.

00:35:58.747 --> 00:36:01.093
I will kill you all!

00:36:01.768 --> 00:36:03.645
Lee!

00:36:13.822 --> 00:36:15.490
Damn.

00:36:20.704 --> 00:36:22.372
Lee!

00:36:24.541 --> 00:36:27.210
Jack, you come with me.

00:36:27.245 --> 00:36:28.670
Missy.

00:36:28.879 --> 00:36:31.298
You watch him now.

00:36:40.140 --> 00:36:41.350
Lee?

00:36:41.641 --> 00:36:43.393
Where are you?

00:36:47.439 --> 00:36:48.899
Lee?

00:36:50.976 --> 00:36:53.562
Damn it. Jack, hit the lights.

00:36:54.896 --> 00:36:57.315
They must have pulled the fuses.

00:38:28.857 --> 00:38:30.558
You stupid...

00:38:31.559 --> 00:38:32.810
Hey!

00:39:08.762 --> 00:39:10.723
I'll watch this one. You go ahead.

00:39:15.402 --> 00:39:17.988
Go ahead.

00:39:28.457 --> 00:39:30.883
You hurt my family.

00:39:30.918 --> 00:39:33.441
I'm gonna bleed you bitch.

00:39:33.476 --> 00:39:35.965
You killed my brother.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:38.342
Your brother?

00:39:39.552 --> 00:39:41.435
Now I see.

00:39:41.470 --> 00:39:44.056
Just tell me why.

00:39:45.567 --> 00:39:48.310
Because it's fun.

00:40:11.174 --> 00:40:11.988
Where's the girl?

00:40:12.023 --> 00:40:13.391
I locked her in the closet.

00:40:13.426 --> 00:40:15.553
What about the dad?

00:40:17.180 --> 00:40:20.809
Shot. Trying to escape.

00:40:31.444 --> 00:40:34.697
I think the car's at the police station.

00:40:34.864 --> 00:40:38.159
Backup units on route to your location.

00:40:40.745 --> 00:40:42.580
So...

00:40:42.914 --> 00:40:46.209
State Police and the FBI are
gonna be here within the hour.

00:40:46.244 --> 00:40:49.128
They're gonna want to talk to you.

00:40:49.629 --> 00:40:53.925
I suggest that you're
both long gone by then.

00:40:54.092 --> 00:40:55.927
Thanks.

00:40:58.137 --> 00:40:59.910
Hey, listen. I don't
mean to press our luck.

00:40:59.945 --> 00:41:01.683
But we're kind of in
the middle of nowhere.

00:41:01.718 --> 00:41:04.060
You think we could catch a ride?

00:41:04.095 --> 00:41:06.354
Start walking.

00:41:07.438 --> 00:41:09.857
Duck if you see a SWAT car.

00:41:09.892 --> 00:41:12.277
Sounds great to me. Thanks.

00:41:12.986 --> 00:41:14.904
Listen...

00:41:16.639 --> 00:41:19.433
I'm sorry about your brother.

00:41:19.892 --> 00:41:21.894
Thank you.

00:41:23.229 --> 00:41:24.779
It was really hard not
knowing what happened to him.

00:41:24.814 --> 00:41:30.319
I thought it would be easier
once I knew the truth. But...

00:41:31.445 --> 00:41:33.864
It isn't really.

00:41:38.703 --> 00:41:41.330
Anyway you should go.

00:41:54.593 --> 00:41:57.096
Don't ever do that again.

00:41:57.131 --> 00:41:58.270
Do what?

00:41:58.305 --> 00:42:00.266
Go missing like that.

00:42:01.684 --> 00:42:03.978
You were worried about me.

00:42:04.729 --> 00:42:08.399
I'm saying, you vanish like that
again I'm not looking for you.

00:42:08.691 --> 00:42:09.711
Sure you will.

00:42:09.746 --> 00:42:10.468
I'm not.

00:42:11.318 --> 00:42:13.577
So you got saddled on by
a 13 year old girl, huh?

00:42:13.612 --> 00:42:14.598
Oh, shut up!

00:42:14.633 --> 00:42:16.570
Just saying getting rusty there, kiddo.

00:42:17.116 --> 00:42:18.784
Shut up!



